[background arg="res://assets/backgrounds/Therapy room.png" fade="0.0"]
set {flags.met_marisol} = true
bea: Marisol Reyes, 11 AM. Writer's block. She brought her own chair cushion.
join marisol (Neutral) leftmost
narrator: She doesn't so much enter as arrive. There's a distinction.
narrator: The cigarette holder has no cigarette. It doesn't need one. It's doing its job.
marisol (Annoyance): "Dr. {game.player_name}."
narrator: The word lands like a ship name.
player: "Ms. Reyes."
marisol (Caring): "Marisol. The pen name is for the books."
narrator: She surveys the office. You can see her filing everything under 'set dressing.'
marisol (Disgust): "It's the block. Three months. Nothing. The words simply..."
narrator: She pauses. Her hand drifts upward.
marisol (Fear): "...refuse to come."
player: "Tell me about the block."
- What were you working on when it started? | [if {stats.knowledge} >= 2] [else="disable" alt_text="need 2 knowledge"]
	marisol: "The Corsair's Surrender. Book seven of the Crimson Tide series."
	narrator: She says it the way other people say "my family."
	player: "What happens in book seven?"
	marisol (Curiosity): "Captain Rodrigo de Valcourt must choose between his oath to the Crimson Brotherhood and the woman who has set fire to his carefully ordered world."
	narrator: A beat.
	marisol (Gratitude): "It's a metaphor."
	do PatientManager.add_therapy("marisol", 5)
	do GameState.add_stat_xp("knowledge", 1)
- What does writer's block feel like, for you?
	marisol: "Like standing at the wheel of a ship with no wind. Everything correct. Everything still."
	narrator: She catches herself.
	marisol: "That's — I apologize. I narrate. It's a professional hazard."
	do PatientManager.add_trust("marisol", 3)
[stat_check stat="perception"]
if {check_result}:
	narrator: She's not distressed. She's performing distress. The cigarette holder spins when she's composing, not when she's suffering — and it's been spinning since she sat down.
	- You don't actually seem that upset about it.
		marisol (Joy): "I beg your—"
		player: "The cigarette holder. It spins when you're thinking, not when you're troubled."
		narrator: A very long pause.
		marisol: "You're more observant than I expected."
		narrator: She doesn't put the holder down. But it stops spinning.
		do PatientManager.add_trust("marisol", 12)
	- Tell me what you do instead of writing.
		marisol (Surprise): "Research. Extensively."
		player: "Into?"
		marisol (Love): "Maritime history. Piracy. The social hierarchies of privateering vessels."
		narrator: She says this with a composure that cannot entirely contain how much she enjoyed saying it.
		do PatientManager.add_trust("marisol", 5)
else:
	- How long have you been a romance novelist?
		marisol: "Eleven years. Six books. The seventh is proving... reluctant."
		narrator: She pronounces it like it's the book's fault.
		do PatientManager.add_trust("marisol", 3)
	- Is there something else going on in your life right now?
		marisol: "In my life. No. In my work, yes. The distinction is important."
		narrator: She says this with great confidence.
		do PatientManager.add_trust("marisol", 2)
narrator: She has been describing a scene — Rodrigo's crisis of faith mid-voyage — for four minutes. You have watched her become, slightly, someone else.
[photo_opportunity id="marisol_swoon" patient="marisol" title="The Swoon" description="Marisol re-enacts a pivotal scene from her seventh novel with complete theatrical commitment, including a practiced swoon onto the therapy couch." portrait="res://assets/photos/marisol/swoon.png"]
if {flags.last_photo_success}:
	narrator: Her expression mid-swoon — eyes closing, one hand to her chest — is, objectively, a lot.
	do PatientManager.add_trust("marisol", 3)
else:
	narrator: By the time you reach for your phone, she's already straightening her jacket.
marisol: "And that's when Rodrigo realizes the oath was never really about the Brotherhood."
narrator: She smooths her jacket with one hand.
marisol: "...Where were we?"
player: "Your block."
marisol (Relief): "Ah. Yes."
narrator: She doesn't look blocked.
[add_note patient="marisol" note="Presents with writer's block. Theatrical throughout — performing distress rather than experiencing it. The fantasy material (pirate-romance, elaborate scenarios) is vivid, immediately accessible, and clearly more alive to her than the problem she came in to discuss."]
leave marisol
do PatientManager.mark_session_done("marisol")
jump between_patients/